course: dictionary
lesson: 3272
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word ermine can name an animal or a material. Context tells you which meaning is meant, so look at the words around it. «In cold northern places a stoat's coat turns white in winter, keeping only the black tail tip; this white fur is called ermine.» Here the stoat is the animal, and ermine is the name for its white winter coat.
explain: Read on for the second meaning. Ermine is also the white fur, with black spots, worn on the robes of kings, queens, judges and lords. A robe trimmed with fur is not an animal, so the sentence tells you which meaning fits. Ask yourself: does this sentence fit an animal, or fur on clothes?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «the judge wore ermine» makes sense, the word means the fur. If «the ermine darted across the snow» makes sense, it means the animal.
fact: Ermine means a stoat in its white winter coat, with a black tip to its tail.
fact: A stoat is a small, long-bodied animal of the weasel family.
fact: Ermine also means the white fur, with black spots, worn on the robes of kings, queens, judges and lords.
fact: In winter a stoat's coat turns white, which helps it hide in the snow.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so always check the context before you decide.
exercise: «In winter the ermine's coat turns white, with only the black tail tip showing.» What is the ermine in this sentence? | A castle on a hill | A kind of snow | *A stoat in its winter coat | A king's robe trimmed with fur
exercise: «The judge's robe was trimmed with ermine.» What is ermine in this sentence? | A small animal that lives by rivers | *The white fur, with black spots, worn on the robe | A type of stone | A cold, wet winter day
exercise: Why does a stoat's coat turn white in winter? | *So it can hide in the snow | So it can swim faster | To keep it warm in the summer | To make it look bigger
test: «The ermine darted across the snowy field.» Which meaning is right here? | A kind of snow | *The animal | A type of weather | The fur on a robe
test: What is the best way to check the meaning of a word with more than one meaning? | Guess the first meaning you think of | Ignore the words around the hard word | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the picture
exam: «The queen's ermine-trimmed robe shone in the hall, while a stoat hid in the snow outside.» In the first part of this sentence, ermine means: | A sort of hall | *White fur with black spots, worn on royal robes | A small river animal | A stoat's white winter coat
